  "bios": {
    "short": "Pipí Ciagi is a multidisciplinary creator from Sabaki — a fashion designer, creative director, and recording artist connected to Culture SZN through key collaborations like “SABAKI” with XiiX.",
    "website": "Pipí Ciagi is a multidisciplinary creator from Sabaki, Kenya, working across fashion and music. As a designer and creative director, he translates street-born energy into intentional silhouettes, texture-forward details, and visual identity built for the now. As a recording artist, he contributes to Culture SZN’s sound through collaborative releases — including his feature on XiiX’s “SABAKI.”\n\nAcross both disciplines, Pipí Ciagi’s work is driven by storytelling and presence: bold choices, sharp execution, and a cultural point of view. Whether building a look or a record, the goal is the same — make the statement undeniable.",
    "press_kit": "Pipí Ciagi (b. 24 May 1996) is a multidisciplinary creator from Sabaki, Kenya — a fashion designer and creative director whose work blends contemporary street aesthetics with intentional craftsmanship, and a recording artist associated with Hip-Hop/Rap. He is connected to Culture SZN’s creative ecosystem through collaborative music credits, including “SABAKI” with XiiX and “GAS N GO” with Culture SZN."
